        "char_length": 973,
        "offset_encoding": "codepoint",
        "exact_quote": "(b) If the RE developer chooses to avail waiver based on proposed sub-clauses (h-\ni and h-ii) based on its start date of connectivity as on date of signing of\nPPA/PSA or SCOD as per PPA/PSA, whichever is later, the project shall be\neligible for waiver of 75% for a period of 10 years i.e. PPA tenure (considering\nbaseline date as 30.04.2026) from its COD. If the RE developer extends the\nsame PPA beyond 10 years , it will continue to be eligible for a waiver of 75%\nmaximum up to 25 years from date of COD. However, after the expiry of the\nterm of the original PPA i.e. 10 Years, if the new PPA is entered with different\nbuyer or in case the original PPA gets terminated (due to any of the reasons)\nbefore expiry of the tenure of the PPA (say during 8th year), the project shall be\neligible for waiver as per trajectory under Table 1 of Regulation 13(2)(a) read\nwith Regulation 13(2)(h) for the balance period (considering the max. waiver\nperiod allowed is for 25 years).\n"
      }
    ],
